---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ExamResizer from '../components/ExamResizer.astro';
import SEOContent from '../components/SEOContent.astro';

const SEO_TITLE = "Photo Resizer for SSC CGL Online - Exact Dimensions (100x120px, 20KB)";
const SEO_DESC = "Automatically resize and compress your photo for SSC CGL to the exact required 100x120 pixels and under 20KB without losing quality.";
---

<Layout title={SEO_TITLE} description={SEO_DESC} showMesh={true}>
  <!-- Tool Section -->
  <section class="relative z-20 pt-16 container-stripe">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <div style="display: inline-block; padding: 6px 16px; background: rgba(200, 241, 53, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(200, 241, 53, 0.3); border-radius: 100px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-lime); margin-bottom: 16px;">
        100% SECURE & CLIENT-SIDE
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.25rem); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Photo Resizer for <span style="color: var(--color-lime);">SSC CGL</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.0625rem; color: var(--color-ink-2); max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.65;">
        Instantly fix the "invalid image dimensions" error. Automatically compress your SSC CGL photograph to the exact 100x120 pixels and required KB limit.
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <ExamResizer defaultExam="ssc" defaultType="photo" allowMultiple={true} />
  </section>

  <!-- SEO Content Section -->
  <SEOContent 
    targetKB="20KB" 
    customTitle="How to Resize Photo for SSC CGL"
    customFaqs={[
      {
        q: "Can I use my mobile phone to take the SSC CGL 2026 photo?",
        a: "Yes, you can use a smartphone, but ensure the background is plain white or light-colored, lighting is even (no shadows on your face), and the camera is held at eye level. Avoid selfie angles and never use filters."
      },
      {
        q: "My photo size is exactly 20 KB. Will it be accepted for SSC CGL?",
        a: "While 20 KB is the exact minimum, it is risky. It's best to aim for a file size between 30 KB and 40 KB so you don't face upload errors on the SSC portal while still adhering to the 20 KB - 50 KB limits."
      },
      {
        q: "Is a date printed on the SSC CGL photo mandatory for 2026?",
        a: "Historically, SSC required the date of taking the photograph to be printed on the image. However, recent notifications have relaxed this rule. Always read the exact SSC CGL 2026 official notification, but typically, a clear photo without the date is accepted as long as it is not older than 3 months."
      },
      {
        q: "What happens if I wear glasses in my SSC CGL photo?",
        a: "Your application will be rejected. SSC strictly prohibits wearing spectacles, sunglasses, or caps in the application photo. Even if you wear prescription glasses daily, you must remove them for the photograph."
      },
      {
        q: "How do I resize my signature for SSC CGL?",
        a: "The signature must be between 10 KB to 20 KB with dimensions of 4.0 cm (width) x 2.0 cm (height). It must be signed on white paper with a black ink pen."
      }
    ]}
    uniqueContent={`
      <p class="seo-p">
        The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) is notoriously strict about application photos. Every year, thousands of capable candidates have their SSC CGL Tier 1 applications rejected because their uploaded photos or signatures fail to meet the exact technical guidelines. Preparing your documents before the SSC online application window opens is the most critical first step.
      </p>

      <h3 class="seo-h3" style="margin-top: 32px;">Exact SSC CGL 2026 Photo & Signature Requirements</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">Before uploading, you must ensure both your photograph and signature strictly adhere to the Staff Selection Commission's official notification guidelines.</p>
      
      <h4 class="seo-h4" style="margin-top: 24px; font-weight: bold; color: var(--color-ink); font-size: 1.125rem;">Photo Specifications:</h4>
      <ul class="seo-p" style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <li><strong>File Size:</strong> Between 20 KB and 50 KB.</li>
        <li><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 3.5 cm (width) x 4.5 cm (height) (or exactly 100x120 pixels).</li>
        <li><strong>Format:</strong> JPEG or JPG only.</li>
        <li><strong>Age:</strong> Must not be more than 3 months old from the date of the exam notification.</li>
        <li><strong>Subject Rules:</strong> Absolutely NO spectacles, caps, or dark glasses. Both ears should be clearly visible.</li>
        <li><strong>Background:</strong> Plain white or very light background.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4 class="seo-h4" style="margin-top: 24px; font-weight: bold; color: var(--color-ink); font-size: 1.125rem;">Signature Specifications:</h4>
      <ul class="seo-p" style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <li><strong>File Size:</strong> Between 10 KB and 20 KB.</li>
        <li><strong>Dimensions:</strong> 4.0 cm (width) x 2.0 cm (height).</li>
        <li><strong>Format:</strong> JPEG/JPG.</li>
        <li><strong>Ink:</strong> Must be signed in black or blue ink on plain white paper.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="seo-h3" style="margin-top: 40px;">Step-by-Step: How to Resize Photo for SSC CGL Application</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">Avoid using generic photo editing software which might compress the photo too much or ruin the aspect ratio. Our specialized SSC CGL Photo Resizer automates this process for you seamlessly:</p>
      <ol class="seo-p" style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <li><strong>Upload Your Image:</strong> Click the upload box or drag and drop your raw, unedited photograph into our client-side tool.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-Crop:</strong> The tool sets the 3.5 cm x 4.5 cm aspect ratio. Adjust the crop box to center your face and ensure both ears are visible.</li>
        <li><strong>Verify Pixel Dimensions:</strong> The resizer automatically scales the image to the required dimensions for the SSC portal.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-Compress to 20KB-50KB:</strong> The engine dynamically compresses the file, guaranteeing the final output strictly falls within the 20 KB to 50 KB limit without losing crucial visual clarity.</li>
        <li><strong>Download & Apply:</strong> Click download. Your file is saved directly to your device, completely ready for the ssc.gov.in portal.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3 class="seo-h3" style="margin-top: 40px;">Common SSC CGL Photo Rejection Reasons</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">Don't let a technicality ruin your chances of securing an Inspector or Assistant Section Officer (ASO) post. SSC strictly defines unacceptable photos. The most frequent reasons for rejection include:</p>
      <ul class="seo-p" style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <li><strong>Wearing Spectacles:</strong> This is the absolute #1 reason for rejection. Even if you wear prescription glasses for vision, you MUST remove them for the photograph. No exceptions.</li>
        <li><strong>Blurry Images:</strong> Over-compressing a photo manually to get it under 50KB can make it illegible. If your facial features are not sharp, the application will be rejected.</li>
        <li><strong>Inverted or Sideways Photos:</strong> Uploading the photo in a horizontal/landscape orientation instead of portrait.</li>
        <li><strong>Selfie Angles:</strong> Selfies distort facial proportions and rarely have a compliant plain background.</li>
        <li><strong>Dark or Cluttered Backgrounds:</strong> Using scenery, dark colored walls, or messy rooms as a backdrop.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="seo-h3" style="margin-top: 40px;">Differences: SSC CGL vs. CHSL vs. MTS Requirements</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">A frequent question among aspirants applying for multiple Staff Selection Commission exams is whether they can reuse the same photo for CGL, CHSL (Combined Higher Secondary Level), and MTS (Multi-Tasking Staff).</p>
      <p class="seo-p">The physical requirements (3.5 x 4.5 cm, 20-50 KB, JPEG format, no spectacles) are practically identical across all major SSC exams conducted on the new ssc.gov.in One Time Registration (OTR) portal. However, always ensure your photo is recent. If you applied for MTS in January and CGL in September, you CANNOT use the same photo, as it violates the strict 3-month recency rule.</p>

      <h3 class="seo-h3" style="margin-top: 40px;">Mobile Camera Tips for the SSC Application Photo</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">You don't need a professional studio to get a compliant photo. You can capture one at home using your smartphone:</p>
      <ul class="seo-p" style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <li><strong>Use Natural Light:</strong> Stand facing a window during the day. Natural light provides even illumination and avoids harsh shadows on your face or the wall.</li>
        <li><strong>Find a Blank Wall:</strong> Stand 1-2 feet away from a plain white or light-colored wall to avoid dropping a hard shadow behind you.</li>
        <li><strong>Clean Your Lens:</strong> A smudged camera lens creates a hazy effect. Wipe it with a cloth before clicking.</li>
        <li><strong>Eye Level Angle:</strong> Have a family member or friend hold the phone exactly at your eye level.</li>
        <li><strong>Neutral Expression:</strong> Keep your mouth closed, don't smile too broadly, and look straight into the lens.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="seo-h3" style="margin-top: 40px;">Important SSC Exam Timelines & New Portal Features</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">With the migration to the new SSC website (ssc.gov.in), candidates are required to complete a One Time Registration (OTR). While a new feature occasionally requires candidates to capture a "Live Photo" using their webcam, a standard uploaded passport-size photo and scanned signature are still mandatory for specific application forms and internal verifications.</p>
      <p class="seo-p">Ensure your digital files are precisely resized before the application window opens. The SSC servers frequently experience extreme load during the final 3-4 days of the application deadline. Having your perfectly sized 20KB-50KB images ready prevents frustrating timeouts and errors during submission.</p>
    `}
  />
</Layout>
